WEBVTT

00:00:05.061 --> 00:00:06.469
Previously on Supernatural

00:00:09.531 --> 00:00:11.511
Take your brother outside
as fast as you  can!

00:00:11.653 --> 00:00:12.633
Now, Dean! Go!

00:00:14.546 --> 00:00:15.750
Mary! No!

00:00:17.852 --> 00:00:18.873
Dad's on a hunting trip.

00:00:20.241 --> 00:00:21.486
And he hasn't been home in a few days.

00:00:23.582 --> 00:00:25.010
I swore I was done hunting.

00:00:25.725 --> 00:00:26.806
I can't do this alone.

00:00:29.413 --> 00:00:30.086
No!

00:00:32.903 --> 00:00:34.025
We got work to do.

00:00:34.692 --> 00:00:37.121
This is dad's single
most valuable possession

00:00:37.162 --> 00:00:39.325
Everything he knows about
every evil thing is in here.

00:00:39.488 --> 00:00:41.407
I think he wants us to
pick up where he left off

00:00:41.529 --> 00:00:43.856
You know, saving people, hunting things,

00:00:43.931 --> 00:00:44.870
Family business.

00:00:44.911 --> 00:00:46.768
No. I got to find Jessica's killer.

00:00:46.788 --> 00:00:48.319
It's the only thing I can think about.

00:00:48.360 --> 00:00:50.136
Sam, You know we're
gonna find dad, right?

00:00:51.966 --> 00:00:52.946
Yeah. I know.

00:01:02.485 --> 00:01:04.403
Okay, your turn. Truth or dare?

00:01:04.826 --> 00:01:05.479
Truth.

00:01:06.540 --> 00:01:08.152
Do you want to make
out with benji swartz?

00:01:09.479 --> 00:01:10.091
Dare.

00:01:10.642 --> 00:01:11.806
Okay, lame.

00:01:12.718 --> 00:01:13.901
You have to...

00:01:14.983 --> 00:01:16.759
Say "bloody mary" in the bathroom.

00:01:17.426 --> 00:01:19.345
Is that the best you can come up with?

00:01:19.712 --> 00:01:20.855
Who's bloody mary?

00:01:21.365 --> 00:01:22.692
She's this witch.

00:01:23.100 --> 00:01:24.958
I heard she was a lady
killed in a car crash.

00:01:25.447 --> 00:01:26.815
It doesn't matter who she is.

00:01:27.267 --> 00:01:29.961
If you say her name three
times in the bathroom mirror,

00:01:30.777 --> 00:01:31.899
She appears...

00:01:32.593 --> 00:01:33.900
And scratches your eyes out!

00:01:36.656 --> 00:01:38.432
So why would anyone say it?

00:01:39.126 --> 00:01:40.616
Because it isn't real.

00:01:42.044 --> 00:01:43.371
No turning on the lights.

00:01:43.990 --> 00:01:44.949
And remember,

00:01:45.112 --> 00:01:45.949
Three times.

00:02:11.765 --> 00:02:12.704
Bloody mary.

00:02:14.520 --> 00:02:15.785
This is so stupid.

00:02:19.791 --> 00:02:20.729
Bloody mary.

00:02:31.423 --> 00:02:32.444
Bloody mary.

00:02:43.146 --> 00:02:43.799
Scared you.

00:02:43.922 --> 00:02:45.105
You guys are jerks.

00:02:45.350 --> 00:02:46.065
Lily?

00:02:46.738 --> 00:02:47.779
You mind keeping it down?

00:02:48.657 --> 00:02:49.657
Sorry, daddy.

00:02:49.800 --> 00:02:51.494
Sorry, mr. Shoemaker.

00:03:29.803 --> 00:03:31.191
You so like him!

00:03:32.960 --> 00:03:33.899
Hey, geek.

00:03:34.144 --> 00:03:35.491
You guys having fun?

00:03:35.818 --> 00:03:37.103
You're out past curfew.

00:03:37.812 --> 00:03:38.669
Thanks, dad.

00:04:20.611 --> 00:04:21.754
Why Sam?

00:04:23.741 --> 00:04:24.353
No!

00:04:27.735 --> 00:04:29.551
Why Sam? Sam, wake up.

00:04:38.363 --> 00:04:40.261
I take it I was having a nightmare?

00:04:41.098 --> 00:04:42.649
Yeah, another one.

00:04:46.276 --> 00:04:47.746
Hey, at least I got some sleep.

00:04:47.909 --> 00:04:50.175
Hey, you know, sooner or later,
we're gonna talk about this.

00:04:51.134 --> 00:04:51.848
Are we here?

00:04:52.256 --> 00:04:54.726
Yep. Welcome to Toledo, Ohio.

00:04:58.421 --> 00:05:00.523
So, what do you think
really happened to this guy?

00:05:00.557 --> 00:05:02.170
So what we're gonna find out.

00:05:04.721 --> 00:05:05.517
Let's go.

00:05:34.742 --> 00:05:35.253
Hey.

00:05:35.987 --> 00:05:36.600
Hey.

00:05:38.008 --> 00:05:38.763
Can I help you?

00:05:39.416 --> 00:05:41.478
Yeah, we're the... med students.

00:05:41.985 --> 00:05:42.557
Sorry?

00:05:42.924 --> 00:05:43.822
Oh, doctor...

00:05:44.455 --> 00:05:46.067
Fliglavitch didn't tell you?

00:05:46.128 --> 00:05:48.026
We talked to him on the phone.

00:05:48.169 --> 00:05:49.394
We're from Ohio state.

00:05:49.700 --> 00:05:51.737
He's supposed to show
us the shoemaker corpse.

00:05:51.758 --> 00:05:52.513
It's for our paper.

00:05:52.778 --> 00:05:54.574
Well, I'm sorry, he's at lunch.

00:05:54.738 --> 00:05:55.391
Oh.

00:05:55.534 --> 00:05:56.615
Well, he said, uh

00:05:56.840 --> 00:05:58.064
Oh, well, you know, it doesn't matter.

00:05:58.900 --> 00:06:00.533
You don't mind showing
us the body, do you?

00:06:00.574 --> 00:06:01.798
Sorry, I can't.

00:06:02.002 --> 00:06:04.268
Doc will be back in an
hour. You can wait for him,

00:06:04.390 --> 00:06:05.023
If you want.

00:06:05.186 --> 00:06:05.941
An hour?

00:06:07.312 --> 00:06:09.046
We got to be heading back to columbus.

00:06:09.108 --> 00:06:09.740
Yeah.

00:06:10.434 --> 00:06:12.087
Look man, this paper's half our grade,

00:06:12.128 --> 00:06:13.904
So if you don't mind
helping us out? Look, man

00:06:15.159 --> 00:06:15.914
No.

00:06:18.302 --> 00:06:20.160
I'm gonna hit him in his face, I swear.

00:06:34.052 --> 00:06:35.093
Follow me.

00:06:38.985 --> 00:06:40.522
Dude, I earned that money.

00:06:40.639 --> 00:06:42.169
You won it in a poker game.

00:06:42.394 --> 00:06:43.190
Yeah.

00:06:43.904 --> 00:06:45.802
The newspaper said
his daughter found him.

00:06:46.204 --> 00:06:47.755
She said his eyes were bleeding.

00:06:47.837 --> 00:06:48.898
More than that.

00:06:48.980 --> 00:06:50.572
They practically liquefied.

00:06:54.367 --> 00:06:57.385
Any sign of a struggle,
maybe somebody did it to him?

00:06:57.566 --> 00:06:58.239
Nope.

00:06:58.648 --> 00:07:00.342
Besides the daughter, he was all alone.

00:07:01.168 --> 00:07:02.805
What's the official causeof death?

00:07:03.390 --> 00:07:05.963
Doc's not sure. He's
thinking massive stroke,

00:07:05.987 --> 00:07:07.554
Maybe an aneurysm.

00:07:08.232 --> 00:07:09.870
Something burst up in
there, that's for sure.

00:07:10.448 --> 00:07:11.337
What do you mean?

00:07:11.828 --> 00:07:13.606
Intense cerebral bleeding.

00:07:13.980 --> 00:07:16.389
This guy had more blooding his
skull than anyone I've ever seen.

00:07:17.325 --> 00:07:18.284
But the eyes?

00:07:18.635 --> 00:07:20.085
What would cause something like that?

00:07:20.283 --> 00:07:21.850
Capillaries can burst.

00:07:21.897 --> 00:07:23.862
See a lot of bloodshot
eyes with stroke victims.

00:07:24.213 --> 00:07:26.341
Yeah, you ever see exploding eyeballs?

00:07:26.879 --> 00:07:28.260
That's a first for me.

00:07:28.377 --> 00:07:30.037
But, hey, I'm not the doctor.

00:07:31.538 --> 00:07:33.644
Think we could take a
look atthat police report?

00:07:33.761 --> 00:07:35.398
You know, for our paper?

00:07:36.264 --> 00:07:38.603
I'm not really supposed to show you

00:07:42.702 --> 00:07:44.199
Might not be one of ours.

00:07:44.293 --> 00:07:46.257
Might just be some freak medical thing.

00:07:46.749 --> 00:07:48.198
How many times in dad's long

00:07:48.199 --> 00:07:51.333
And varied career has it actually
been a freak medical thing

00:07:51.560 --> 00:07:54.554
And not some sign of an
awful supernatural death?

00:07:54.694 --> 00:07:56.636
Uh, almost never.

00:07:56.823 --> 00:07:57.829
Exactly.

00:07:57.946 --> 00:07:58.811
All right.

00:07:59.115 --> 00:08:00.628
Let's go talk to the daughter.

00:08:10.010 --> 00:08:11.414
Feel like we're underdressed.

00:08:29.761 --> 00:08:31.087
You must be Donna,right?

00:08:31.274 --> 00:08:31.883
Yeah.

00:08:33.590 --> 00:08:35.859
Hi, uh... We're really sorry.

00:08:36.748 --> 00:08:37.520
Thank you.

00:08:38.035 --> 00:08:39.976
I'm sam.This is dean.

00:08:40.871 --> 00:08:42.134
We worked with your dad.

00:08:43.467 --> 00:08:44.262
You did?

00:08:44.590 --> 00:08:45.830
Yeah.This whole thing

00:08:46.625 --> 00:08:47.795
I mean, a stroke.

00:08:49.381 --> 00:08:51.322
I don't think she really wants
to talk about this right now.

00:08:51.323 --> 00:08:52.609
It's okay, I'm okay.

00:08:54.294 --> 00:08:55.674
Were there ever any symptoms?

00:08:55.791 --> 00:08:57.078
Dizziness, migraines?

00:08:58.154 --> 00:08:59.019
No.

00:09:00.233 --> 00:09:02.175
That's because it wasn't a stroke.

00:09:02.409 --> 00:09:03.415
Lily, don't say that.

00:09:03.672 --> 00:09:04.374
What?

00:09:05.169 --> 00:09:06.666
I'm sorry, she's just upset.

00:09:06.900 --> 00:09:08.654
No, it happened because of me.

00:09:08.725 --> 00:09:09.988
Sweetie, it didn't.

00:09:10.069 --> 00:09:10.865
Lily,

00:09:11.866 --> 00:09:13.621
Why would you saysomething like that?

00:09:14.559 --> 00:09:16.173
Right before he died,I said it.

00:09:16.875 --> 00:09:17.694
You said what?

00:09:18.419 --> 00:09:20.922
Bloody Mary, three times
in the bathroom mirror.

00:09:24.353 --> 00:09:26.014
She took his eyes, that's what she does.

00:09:26.084 --> 00:09:28.494
That's not why dad
died.This isn't your fault.

00:09:29.219 --> 00:09:30.739
I think your sister's right,lily.

00:09:31.621 --> 00:09:33.749
There's no way it could
have been Bloody Mary.

00:09:34.896 --> 00:09:37.118
Your dad didn't say it,did he?

00:09:38.849 --> 00:09:40.322
No, I don't think so.

00:10:05.615 --> 00:10:06.972
Sam:The Bloody Mary legend

00:10:08.808 --> 00:10:11.299
Dad ever find any evidence
that it was a real thing?

00:10:12.094 --> 00:10:13.357
Not that I know of.

00:10:18.602 --> 00:10:19.397
I mean,

00:10:19.912 --> 00:10:20.988
Everywhere else,

00:10:22.080 --> 00:10:26.126
All over the country,
kids will play Bloody Mary.

00:10:26.127 --> 00:10:28.373
And as far as we know,
nobody dies from it.

00:10:28.420 --> 00:10:30.209
Hey well, maybe everywhere
it's just a story,

00:10:30.232 --> 00:10:31.846
But here it's actually happening.

00:10:31.940 --> 00:10:33.530
The place where the legend began?

00:10:34.856 --> 00:10:37.079
But according to the legend,
the person who says...

00:10:40.166 --> 00:10:42.880
The person who says
you know what gets it

00:10:42.903 --> 00:10:43.488
But here...

00:10:43.511 --> 00:10:45.055
Shoemaker gets it instead,yeah.

00:10:45.102 --> 00:10:45.710
Right.

00:10:46.739 --> 00:10:48.540
Never heard anything like that before.

00:10:49.352 --> 00:10:51.832
Still, the guy did die
right in front of the mirror.

00:10:52.031 --> 00:10:54.229
And the daughter's right.
The way the legend goes,

00:10:54.924 --> 00:10:56.772
"You know who" scratches your eyes out.

00:10:56.936 --> 00:10:58.292
It's worth checking into.

00:11:05.380 --> 00:11:06.479
What are you doingup here?

00:11:07.819 --> 00:11:08.590
We...

00:11:09.175 --> 00:11:10.555
We had to go to the bathroom.

00:11:11.585 --> 00:11:12.520
Who are you?

00:11:13.620 --> 00:11:16.076
Like we said downstairs,
we worked with Donna's dad.

00:11:16.380 --> 00:11:18.953
He was a day trader or
something, he worked by himself.

00:11:19.236 --> 00:11:20.733
No, I know, I meant...

00:11:20.896 --> 00:11:22.955
And those weird questions downstairs,

00:11:23.914 --> 00:11:24.990
What was that?

00:11:27.072 --> 00:11:28.896
So you tell me what's going on

00:11:29.508 --> 00:11:30.654
Or I start screaming.

00:11:30.888 --> 00:11:32.011
All right, all right.

00:11:34.329 --> 00:11:36.411
We think something
happened to Donna's dad.

00:11:36.528 --> 00:11:37.604
Yeah, a stroke.

00:11:37.931 --> 00:11:39.756
That's not the sign of a typical stroke.

00:11:42.142 --> 00:11:43.639
We think it might be something else.

00:11:44.364 --> 00:11:45.129
Like what?

00:11:45.760 --> 00:11:46.743
Honestly,

00:11:47.936 --> 00:11:48.965
We don't know yet.

00:11:50.088 --> 00:11:52.193
But we don't want it to
happen to anyone else.

00:11:52.661 --> 00:11:53.496
That's the truth.

00:11:54.408 --> 00:11:55.063
So,

00:11:55.601 --> 00:11:56.794
If you're gonna scream,

00:11:57.590 --> 00:11:58.736
Go right ahead.

00:12:01.332 --> 00:12:02.331
Who are you, cops?

00:12:04.857 --> 00:12:05.746
Something like that.

00:12:05.840 --> 00:12:06.869
I'll tell you what.

00:12:07.126 --> 00:12:07.781
Here.

00:12:08.249 --> 00:12:09.477
If you think of anything,

00:12:09.547 --> 00:12:11.489
You or your friends
notice anything strange,

00:12:11.769 --> 00:12:14.062
Out of the ordinary,
just give us a call.

00:12:22.529 --> 00:12:24.627
All right, say Bloody Mary
really is haunting this town.

00:12:24.651 --> 00:12:26.639
There's gonna be some sort of proof

00:12:26.733 --> 00:12:28.136
A local woman who died nasty.

00:12:28.276 --> 00:12:30.171
Yeah, but a legend this
wide spread, it's hard.

00:12:30.194 --> 00:12:32.532
I mean, there's like 50
versions of who she actually is.

00:12:32.533 --> 00:12:33.690
One story says she's a witch,

00:12:33.691 --> 00:12:35.866
Another says she's a mutilated bride.

00:12:35.960 --> 00:12:36.989
There's a lot more.

00:12:37.130 --> 00:12:38.720
What are we supposed to be looking for?

00:12:38.854 --> 00:12:40.679
Every version's got thingsin common.

00:12:40.702 --> 00:12:41.918
It's always a woman named Mary,

00:12:41.930 --> 00:12:44.035
And she always dies
in front of a mirror.

00:12:44.550 --> 00:12:46.251
So we've got to search local newspapers

00:12:46.274 --> 00:12:48.192
Public records as far back as they go,

00:12:48.286 --> 00:12:50.157
See if we can find a
Mary who fits the bill.

00:12:50.789 --> 00:12:51.888
Well, that sounds annoying.

00:12:52.075 --> 00:12:53.689
No, it won't be so bad,

00:12:53.759 --> 00:12:54.718
As long as we...

00:12:56.690 --> 00:12:57.556
I take it back.

00:12:58.234 --> 00:12:59.661
This will be very annoying.

00:13:02.702 --> 00:13:05.848
I'm not sure. They were cops
or detectives or something.

00:13:06.129 --> 00:13:08.047
Whoever they were, they were cute.

00:13:08.164 --> 00:13:08.912
Jill.

00:13:09.029 --> 00:13:09.989
You didn't think so?

00:13:10.224 --> 00:13:12.025
Yeah, okay,they were cute. But,

00:13:12.836 --> 00:13:15.760
Still,do you think something
could have happenedto Donna's dad?

00:13:15.894 --> 00:13:17.280
Maybe Lily was right.

00:13:17.882 --> 00:13:19.730
Maybe Bloody Mary got him.

00:13:20.666 --> 00:13:21.665
Very funny.

00:13:22.811 --> 00:13:24.729
Wait, I'm sorry.

00:13:25.454 --> 00:13:27.653
Was that fear I hear in your voice?

00:13:28.261 --> 00:13:29.033
No.

00:13:30.359 --> 00:13:31.178
Charlie...

00:13:31.412 --> 00:13:33.260
I'm walking to the
bathroom mirror right now.

00:13:34.149 --> 00:13:35.295
Jill, quit it.

00:13:38.003 --> 00:13:39.032
Oh, no,

00:13:39.383 --> 00:13:40.670
I can't help myself.

00:13:41.535 --> 00:13:42.822
I'm gonna say it.

00:13:43.898 --> 00:13:44.857
Bloody Mary.

00:13:45.692 --> 00:13:47.072
Bloody Mary.

00:13:48.055 --> 00:13:49.973
Bloody Mary.

00:13:52.352 --> 00:13:53.171
Jill?

00:13:58.107 --> 00:13:58.878
Jill!

00:14:03.422 --> 00:14:05.574
You're such a freak.
I'll call you tomorrow.

00:15:01.175 --> 00:15:02.321
You did it.

00:15:07.257 --> 00:15:08.695
You killed that boy.

00:15:28.741 --> 00:15:29.654
Why Sam?

00:15:34.581 --> 00:15:35.985
Why'd you let me fall asleep?

00:15:36.570 --> 00:15:38.207
'Cause I'm an awesome brother.

00:15:40.317 --> 00:15:41.790
So, what did you dream about?

00:15:42.562 --> 00:15:44.387
Lollipops and candy canes.

00:15:46.094 --> 00:15:47.170
Yeah, sure.

00:15:51.605 --> 00:15:52.774
You find anything?

00:15:53.078 --> 00:15:55.464
Oh, besides a whole new
level of frustration?

00:15:55.979 --> 00:15:58.061
No. I've looked at everything.

00:16:00.158 --> 00:16:02.615
A few local women, a
Laura and a Catherine,

00:16:02.638 --> 00:16:04.463
Committed suicide in front of a mirror,

00:16:04.884 --> 00:16:06.935
And a giant mirror fell
on a guy named dave.

00:16:07.029 --> 00:16:07.918
But, uh...

00:16:09.064 --> 00:16:09.836
No Mary.

00:16:14.163 --> 00:16:15.824
Maybe we just haven't found it yet.

00:16:17.087 --> 00:16:19.192
I've also been searching
for strange deaths,

00:16:19.276 --> 00:16:20.843
In the area, you know,

00:16:21.197 --> 00:16:22.858
Eyeball bleeding, that sort of thing.

00:16:22.998 --> 00:16:24.027
There's nothing.

00:16:24.869 --> 00:16:26.834
Whatever's happening here,
maybe it just ain't Mary.

00:16:33.337 --> 00:16:34.039
Hello?

00:16:41.511 --> 00:16:44.295
And they found her
on the bathroom floor.

00:16:45.441 --> 00:16:48.435
And her-Her eyes...

00:16:49.956 --> 00:16:51.430
They were gone.

00:16:52.295 --> 00:16:53.161
I'm sorry.

00:16:55.453 --> 00:16:56.576
And she said it.

00:16:58.447 --> 00:16:59.937
I heard her say it.

00:17:01.500 --> 00:17:03.152
But it couldn't be because of that.

00:17:06.534 --> 00:17:07.633
I'm insane, right?

00:17:09.545 --> 00:17:10.644
No, you're not insane.

00:17:11.673 --> 00:17:14.457
God, that makes me feel so much worse.

00:17:15.432 --> 00:17:16.227
Look...

00:17:19.549 --> 00:17:21.245
We think something's happening here,

00:17:22.485 --> 00:17:24.075
Something that can't be explained.

00:17:25.191 --> 00:17:26.244
And we're gonna stop it,

00:17:27.437 --> 00:17:28.513
But we could use your help.

00:17:47.081 --> 00:17:48.578
What did you tell Jill's mom?

00:17:48.625 --> 00:17:51.245
I just said I needed some time alone
with Jill's pictures and things.

00:17:51.278 --> 00:17:51.980
Great.

00:17:52.471 --> 00:17:53.734
I hate lying to her.

00:17:54.389 --> 00:17:55.746
This is for the greater good.

00:17:55.793 --> 00:17:56.775
Hit the lights.

00:18:01.072 --> 00:18:02.499
What are you guys looking for?

00:18:02.990 --> 00:18:04.784
We'll let you know
as soon as we find it.

00:18:04.854 --> 00:18:06.164
Hey, night vision.

00:18:08.036 --> 00:18:09.696
Thanks. Perfect.

00:18:12.974 --> 00:18:14.284
Do I look like Paris Hilton?

00:18:25.969 --> 00:18:27.700
So, I don't get it.

00:18:27.724 --> 00:18:30.133
I mean, the first victim
didn't summon Mary,

00:18:30.157 --> 00:18:31.794
And the second victim did.

00:18:32.145 --> 00:18:33.431
How's she choosing them?

00:18:33.969 --> 00:18:34.695
Beats me.

00:18:39.257 --> 00:18:41.245
I want to know why Jill
said it in the first place.

00:18:42.415 --> 00:18:43.444
It's just a joke.

00:18:43.811 --> 00:18:46.688
Somebody's gonna say it again.
It's just a matter of time.

00:18:59.372 --> 00:19:00.051
Hey.

00:19:01.470 --> 00:19:02.897
There's a black light
in the trunk, right?

00:19:25.591 --> 00:19:27.299
Gary Bryman?

00:19:28.936 --> 00:19:30.163
You know who that is?

00:19:31.560 --> 00:19:32.222
No.

00:19:40.021 --> 00:19:43.202
So, Gary Bryman was an 8 year-Old boy.

00:19:44.115 --> 00:19:46.197
Two years ago, he was
killed in a hit and run.

00:19:46.220 --> 00:19:49.121
The car was described
as a black toyota camry,

00:19:49.722 --> 00:19:52.178
But nobody got the
plates or saw the driver.

00:19:52.506 --> 00:19:53.348
Oh, my god.

00:19:54.307 --> 00:19:54.915
What?

00:19:55.359 --> 00:19:56.763
Jill drove that car.

00:19:59.975 --> 00:20:01.729
We need to get back to
your friend Donna's house.

00:20:10.650 --> 00:20:12.311
Linda shoemaker.

00:20:15.820 --> 00:20:17.177
Why are you asking me this?

00:20:17.539 --> 00:20:19.567
Look, we're sorry, but it's important.

00:20:20.666 --> 00:20:21.321
Yeah.

00:20:21.622 --> 00:20:22.956
Linda's my mom, okay?

00:20:23.283 --> 00:20:25.178
And she overdosed on sleeping pills.

00:20:25.295 --> 00:20:26.979
It was an accident, and that's it.

00:20:30.311 --> 00:20:31.270
I think you should leave.

00:20:31.293 --> 00:20:33.071
Donna, just listen Get out of my house!

00:20:37.392 --> 00:20:38.304
Oh, my god.

00:20:39.591 --> 00:20:42.222
Do you really think her dad
could have killed her mom?

00:20:43.603 --> 00:20:44.538
Maybe.

00:20:45.151 --> 00:20:46.531
I think I should stick around.

00:20:48.168 --> 00:20:49.805
All right. Whatever you do, don't...

00:20:49.993 --> 00:20:52.308
Believe me, I won't say it.

00:20:56.618 --> 00:20:57.811
Wait, wait, wait.

00:20:58.116 --> 00:21:00.057
You're doing a nationwide search?

00:21:00.197 --> 00:21:00.829
Yep.

00:21:01.430 --> 00:21:03.675
The NCIC, the FBI database

00:21:03.868 --> 00:21:07.084
Any mary in the country who died in
front of a mirror is good enough for me.

00:21:07.494 --> 00:21:10.464
But if she's haunting the town,
she should have died in the town.

00:21:10.623 --> 00:21:13.547
I'm telling you. There's nothing local. I
check. So, unless you've gota better idea.

00:21:13.659 --> 00:21:16.003
Why Mary's choosing a victim?
It seems like there's a pattern.

00:21:16.043 --> 00:21:17.245
I know I was thinking the same thing.

00:21:17.325 --> 00:21:19.329
With mr. Shoemaker
and Jill's hit and run

00:21:19.349 --> 00:21:20.871
Both had secrets where people died.

00:21:20.931 --> 00:21:21.432
Right.

00:21:21.512 --> 00:21:22.896
There's a lot of folklore about mirrors

00:21:22.897 --> 00:21:24.900
That they reveal or your
lies, or your secrets,

00:21:24.940 --> 00:21:27.023
That they're a true
reflection of your soul,

00:21:27.024 --> 00:21:28.466
Which is why it's bad
luck to break them.

00:21:28.546 --> 00:21:29.408
Right. Right.

00:21:30.282 --> 00:21:31.644
Yeah, so maybe if you've got a secret,

00:21:31.664 --> 00:21:33.498
I mean, like a really nasty
one where someone died,

00:21:33.499 --> 00:21:35.903
Then mary sees it and
punishes you for it.

00:21:36.035 --> 00:21:37.736
Whether you summoned her or not.

00:21:38.619 --> 00:21:39.601
Take a look at this.

00:21:52.305 --> 00:21:53.908
Looks like the same handprint.

00:21:54.370 --> 00:21:56.073
Her name was Mary Worthington

00:21:56.896 --> 00:21:59.120
An unsolved murder in
Fort Wayne, Indiana.

00:22:01.346 --> 00:22:04.131
I was on the job for 35 years,

00:22:04.371 --> 00:22:05.653
Detective for most of that.

00:22:06.414 --> 00:22:08.778
Now, everybody packs it
in with a few loose ends,

00:22:08.861 --> 00:22:10.784
But the Mary Worthington murder...

00:22:12.647 --> 00:22:14.030
That one still gets me.

00:22:14.250 --> 00:22:15.432
What exactly happened?

00:22:16.896 --> 00:22:18.619
You boys said you were reporters.

00:22:18.980 --> 00:22:20.542
We know Mary was 19,

00:22:20.685 --> 00:22:21.787
Lived by herself.

00:22:21.927 --> 00:22:23.730
We know she won a few beauty contests,

00:22:23.790 --> 00:22:25.252
Dreamt of getting out of Indiana,

00:22:25.773 --> 00:22:26.715
Being an actress.

00:22:27.214 --> 00:22:29.258
And we know, the night of march 29th,

00:22:29.779 --> 00:22:31.161
Someone broke into her apartment

00:22:31.301 --> 00:22:32.143
And murdered her,

00:22:33.064 --> 00:22:34.266
Cut out her eyeswith a knife.

00:22:36.111 --> 00:22:36.872
That's right.

00:22:38.996 --> 00:22:41.240
See, sir, when we ask you what
happened, we want to know what

00:22:41.620 --> 00:22:42.401
You think happened.

00:22:45.971 --> 00:22:48.956
Technically, I'm not supposed
to have a copy of this.

00:22:55.106 --> 00:22:55.707
Now,

00:22:57.310 --> 00:22:58.371
See that there,

00:22:58.952 --> 00:22:59.794

"T-R-E"?

00:23:00.295 --> 00:23:00.916
Yeah.

00:23:01.647 --> 00:23:04.333
I think Mary was trying to
spell out the name of her killer.

00:23:04.414 --> 00:23:05.395
You know who it was?

00:23:05.816 --> 00:23:06.838
Not for sure.

00:23:08.340 --> 00:23:09.722
But there was a local man,

00:23:09.803 --> 00:23:10.684
A surgeon,

00:23:11.247 --> 00:23:12.269
Trevor Sampson.

00:23:12.990 --> 00:23:14.833
And I think he cut her up good.

00:23:15.314 --> 00:23:17.372
Now, why would he do
something like that?

00:23:17.913 --> 00:23:20.096
Her diary mentioned
a man she was seeing.

00:23:20.860 --> 00:23:22.723
She called him by his initial, "T."

00:23:23.524 --> 00:23:24.226
Well,

00:23:24.887 --> 00:23:26.590
Her last entry,

00:23:26.970 --> 00:23:29.915
She was gonna tell to his
wife about their affair.

00:23:30.137 --> 00:23:32.240
But how do you know it
was Sampson who killed her?

00:23:32.862 --> 00:23:34.164
It's hard to say.

00:23:36.750 --> 00:23:39.735
But the way her eyes were cut
out, it was almost professional.

00:23:40.897 --> 00:23:42.321
But you could never prove it?

00:23:42.442 --> 00:23:42.962
No.

00:23:43.443 --> 00:23:44.265
No prints,

00:23:44.365 --> 00:23:45.547
No witnesses.

00:23:46.388 --> 00:23:47.570
He was meticulous.

00:23:49.333 --> 00:23:50.395
Is he still alive?

00:23:52.236 --> 00:23:52.817
Nope.

00:23:55.642 --> 00:23:56.743
If you ask me,

00:23:57.124 --> 00:24:00.109
Mary spent her last living moments

00:24:00.572 --> 00:24:02.876
Trying to expose this guy's secret.

00:24:05.020 --> 00:24:06.222
But she never could.

00:24:08.385 --> 00:24:09.347
Where's she buried?

00:24:10.893 --> 00:24:11.695
She wasn't.

00:24:12.135 --> 00:24:12.937
She was cremated.

00:24:16.342 --> 00:24:19.027
What about that mirror?  It's not
in evidence lockup somewhere, is it?

00:24:20.847 --> 00:24:21.588
No.

00:24:22.890 --> 00:24:25.415
It was returned to Mary's
family a long time ago.

00:24:27.037 --> 00:24:29.121
You have the names of
her family by any chance?

00:24:34.391 --> 00:24:36.356
I mean, you bring these
strangers into my house,

00:24:36.376 --> 00:24:37.919
And they ask me things like that?

00:24:37.959 --> 00:24:39.261
They were only trying to help.

00:24:39.361 --> 00:24:41.425
Please, Donna, you have to believe me.

00:24:41.625 --> 00:24:43.408
What? About bloody mary?

00:24:43.650 --> 00:24:45.774
Please, I know it sounds crazy.

00:24:46.134 --> 00:24:48.057
"Crazy" doesn't even begin to cover it.

00:24:48.278 --> 00:24:50.421
I mean, it's one thing for my
sister to believe this crap.

00:24:50.523 --> 00:24:52.367
She's 12. But you?

00:24:52.889 --> 00:24:53.851
Think about the way

00:24:54.632 --> 00:24:55.553
Your dad died,

00:24:55.994 --> 00:24:58.058
Okay, and the way Jill died.

00:24:59.382 --> 00:25:00.965
Okay, so...

00:25:02.107 --> 00:25:02.667
Bloody Mary.

00:25:02.708 --> 00:25:03.068
No!

00:25:03.108 --> 00:25:05.011
Bloody Mary. Bloody Mary.

00:25:07.978 --> 00:25:09.861
See? Nothing happened.

00:25:10.322 --> 00:25:11.604
Why would you do that?

00:25:12.145 --> 00:25:13.127
Oh, my god,

00:25:13.728 --> 00:25:15.751
There really is
something wrong with you.

00:25:27.627 --> 00:25:30.572
Elements that lose electrons become

00:25:30.712 --> 00:25:32.055
Positive ions,

00:25:32.596 --> 00:25:35.701
Which are smaller than other
atoms of the same element.

00:25:36.222 --> 00:25:38.766
Therefore, the ionic radius

00:25:38.897 --> 00:25:41.201
Is smaller than the atomic radius

00:25:46.435 --> 00:25:47.276
Charlie!

00:25:52.106 --> 00:25:52.868
Charlie!

00:25:57.818 --> 00:26:00.747
Charlie, stop it! What's
wrong? Just calm down!

00:26:03.855 --> 00:26:05.134
Charlie! Aah! Let me go!

00:26:05.264 --> 00:26:06.024
Charlie!

00:26:08.323 --> 00:26:09.065
Oh, really?

00:26:09.529 --> 00:26:11.642
Ah, that's too bad, Mr. Worthington.

00:26:12.208 --> 00:26:13.951
I would have paid a lot for that mirror.

00:26:13.988 --> 00:26:15.231
Okay, well, maybe next time.

00:26:15.453 --> 00:26:16.640
All right, thanks.

00:26:16.788 --> 00:26:17.493
So?

00:26:17.697 --> 00:26:19.551
So, that was Mary's brother.

00:26:19.727 --> 00:26:22.045
The mirror was in the family for years,

00:26:22.101 --> 00:26:23.436
Until he sold it

00:26:23.695 --> 00:26:24.789
One week ago

00:26:25.883 --> 00:26:27.867
To a store called estate antiques,

00:26:28.303 --> 00:26:29.861
A store in Toledo.

00:26:31.715 --> 00:26:33.755
So wherever the mirror
goes, that's where Mary goes?

00:26:34.005 --> 00:26:36.397
Her spirit's definitely
tied up with it somehow.

00:26:36.527 --> 00:26:39.512
Isn't there an old superstition that
says mirrors can capture spirits?

00:26:40.097 --> 00:26:42.285
Yeah, there is. When
someone would die in a house,

00:26:42.322 --> 00:26:44.825
People would cover up the mirrors
so the ghost wouldn't get trapped.

00:26:45.328 --> 00:26:47.561
This Mary dies in front of the
mirror, and it draws in her spirit.

00:26:47.850 --> 00:26:50.835
Yeah, but how could she move
through 100 different mirrors?

00:26:51.484 --> 00:26:53.014
I don't know but if the
mirror is the source,

00:26:53.033 --> 00:26:54.572
I say we find it and smash it.

00:26:55.925 --> 00:26:57.464
Yeah, I don't know. Maybe.

00:27:01.678 --> 00:27:02.327
Hello?

00:27:03.773 --> 00:27:04.496
Charlie?

00:27:23.557 --> 00:27:24.298
Hey.

00:27:25.244 --> 00:27:26.264
Hey. It's okay.

00:27:27.061 --> 00:27:28.767
You can open up your eyes, Charlie.

00:27:28.814 --> 00:27:30.575
It's okay, all right?

00:27:31.929 --> 00:27:32.745
Now, listen.

00:27:33.431 --> 00:27:34.729
You're gonna stay right here

00:27:35.331 --> 00:27:36.129
On this bed.

00:27:36.731 --> 00:27:38.178
You're not gonna look at glass

00:27:38.345 --> 00:27:40.347
Or anything else that
has a reflection, okay?

00:27:41.155 --> 00:27:42.341
As long as you do that

00:27:43.157 --> 00:27:44.585
She cannot get you.

00:27:47.691 --> 00:27:49.471
But I can't keep that up forever.

00:27:52.314 --> 00:27:53.798
I'm gonna die, aren't I?

00:27:55.707 --> 00:27:56.301
No.

00:27:57.895 --> 00:27:58.581
No.

00:28:00.371 --> 00:28:01.548
Not anytime soon.

00:28:03.746 --> 00:28:04.784
All right, Charlie,

00:28:05.470 --> 00:28:06.527
We need to know what happened.

00:28:07.510 --> 00:28:08.826
We were in the bathroom.

00:28:09.077 --> 00:28:09.967
Donna said it.

00:28:10.004 --> 00:28:11.561
That's not what we're talking about.

00:28:15.029 --> 00:28:16.586
Something happened, didn't it,

00:28:18.014 --> 00:28:19.015
In your life.

00:28:20.867 --> 00:28:21.645
A secret...

00:28:22.906 --> 00:28:24.140
Where someone got hurt?

00:28:30.110 --> 00:28:31.436
Can you tell us about it?

00:28:35.553 --> 00:28:36.721
I had this boyfriend.

00:28:39.680 --> 00:28:40.570
I loved him.

00:28:42.387 --> 00:28:44.681
But he kind of scared me, too, you know?

00:28:45.690 --> 00:28:46.560
And...

00:28:46.815 --> 00:28:47.729
One night

00:28:48.281 --> 00:28:49.428
At his house,

00:28:49.746 --> 00:28:50.893
We got in this fight.

00:28:53.293 --> 00:28:54.716
Then I broke up with him,

00:28:55.905 --> 00:28:58.093
And he got upset and he said

00:28:58.369 --> 00:29:00.726
He needed me and he loved me.

00:29:02.224 --> 00:29:03.179
And he said...

00:29:04.220 --> 00:29:07.130
"Charlie, if you walk out that door
right now, I'm gonna kill myself."

00:29:09.997 --> 00:29:11.441
And you know what I said?

00:29:13.061 --> 00:29:14.335
I said, "go ahead."

00:29:17.351 --> 00:29:18.562
And I left.

00:29:21.769 --> 00:29:23.107
How could I say that?

00:29:28.406 --> 00:29:30.254
How could I leave him like that?

00:29:33.340 --> 00:29:34.444
I just...

00:29:35.230 --> 00:29:37.142
I didn't believe him, you know?

00:29:44.043 --> 00:29:45.211
I should have.

00:29:54.336 --> 00:29:57.331
Her boyfriend killing himself,
that's not really Charlie's fault.

00:29:58.244 --> 00:29:59.369
You know as well as I do,

00:29:59.391 --> 00:30:02.131
Spirits don't exactly
see shades of gray,

00:30:02.194 --> 00:30:02.980
Dean.

00:30:03.373 --> 00:30:04.541
Charlie had a secret,

00:30:04.838 --> 00:30:05.815
Someone died.

00:30:06.367 --> 00:30:07.514
That's good enough for Mary.

00:30:08.321 --> 00:30:09.298
I guess.

00:30:09.957 --> 00:30:11.167
You know,I've been thinking,

00:30:12.112 --> 00:30:14.809
It might not be enough
to just smash that mirror.

00:30:15.404 --> 00:30:16.466
Why, what do you mean?

00:30:16.742 --> 00:30:18.059
Mary's hard to pin down, right?

00:30:18.123 --> 00:30:19.822
And she moves around
from mirror to mirror.

00:30:19.843 --> 00:30:22.829
So, who's to say that she's not gonna
just keep hiding in them forever?

00:30:24.252 --> 00:30:25.441
So maybe...

00:30:26.737 --> 00:30:28.245
We should try to pin her down,

00:30:29.356 --> 00:30:31.565
You know, summon her to her mirror

00:30:32.415 --> 00:30:33.604
And then smash it.

00:30:34.241 --> 00:30:35.622
Well, how do you know that's gonna work?

00:30:35.686 --> 00:30:36.471
I don't,

00:30:37.172 --> 00:30:38.383
I'm not for sure.

00:30:40.993 --> 00:30:42.352
Well, who's gonnasummon her?

00:30:44.157 --> 00:30:44.901
I will.

00:30:47.046 --> 00:30:48.299
She'll come after me.

00:30:50.242 --> 00:30:52.111
All right, you know what? That's it.

00:31:02.349 --> 00:31:03.730
This is about Jessica, isn't it?

00:31:07.935 --> 00:31:09.252
You think that's your
dirty little secret,

00:31:09.273 --> 00:31:11.100
That you killed her somehow?

00:31:14.345 --> 00:31:16.511
Sam, this has got to stop, man.

00:31:18.146 --> 00:31:18.953
I mean,

00:31:19.315 --> 00:31:20.674
The nightmares and-And

00:31:20.790 --> 00:31:22.808
Calling her name out in
the middle of the night,

00:31:23.615 --> 00:31:24.974
It's gonna kill you.

00:31:26.291 --> 00:31:27.353
Now, listen to me.

00:31:28.755 --> 00:31:30.241
It wasn't your fault.

00:31:31.715 --> 00:31:34.519
If you want to blame something,
then blame the thing that killed her.

00:31:34.986 --> 00:31:36.473
Or, hell, why don't
you take a swing at me?

00:31:36.515 --> 00:31:39.000
I'm the one that dragged you
away from her the first place.

00:31:39.213 --> 00:31:40.360
I don't blame you.

00:31:40.905 --> 00:31:42.200
You shouldn't blame yourself,

00:31:42.625 --> 00:31:44.260
Because there's
nothingyou could've done.

00:31:44.409 --> 00:31:46.108
I could've warned her. About what?!

00:31:46.899 --> 00:31:48.556
You didn't know what was gonna happen.

00:31:50.000 --> 00:31:51.104
And, besides,

00:31:51.274 --> 00:31:53.366
All of this isn't a secret.
I mean, I know all about it.

00:31:53.377 --> 00:31:54.906
It's not gonna work with Mary anyway.

00:31:55.235 --> 00:31:56.234
No, you don't.

00:31:57.720 --> 00:31:58.294
I don't what?

00:31:58.379 --> 00:32:00.630
You don't know all about it.

00:32:01.352 --> 00:32:02.775
I haven't told you everything.

00:32:04.943 --> 00:32:06.005
What are you talking about?

00:32:06.833 --> 00:32:08.978
It wouldn't really be a
secret if I told you, would it?

00:32:16.207 --> 00:32:16.950
No.

00:32:18.373 --> 00:32:19.414
I don't like it.

00:32:19.435 --> 00:32:20.986
It's not gonna happen. Forget it.

00:32:21.708 --> 00:32:23.917
Dean, that girl back
there is going to die

00:32:24.972 --> 00:32:26.777
Unless we do something about it.

00:32:27.563 --> 00:32:28.349
And you know what?

00:32:28.731 --> 00:32:31.641
Who knows how many more people
are gonna die after that?

00:32:33.107 --> 00:32:34.190
Now, we're doing this.

00:32:37.025 --> 00:32:39.213
You've got to let me do this.

00:33:06.813 --> 00:33:09.043
Well, that's just great.

00:33:18.834 --> 00:33:20.427
All right, let's start looking.

00:33:59.250 --> 00:34:00.822
Maybe they've already sold it.

00:34:06.525 --> 00:34:07.672
I don't think so.

00:34:20.304 --> 00:34:21.303
That's it.

00:34:24.361 --> 00:34:25.572
You sure about this?

00:34:42.467 --> 00:34:43.444
Bloody Mary.

00:34:46.545 --> 00:34:47.607
Bloody Mary.

00:34:59.223 --> 00:35:00.052
Bloody Mary.

00:35:10.360 --> 00:35:12.251
I'll go check that out.
Stay here. Be careful.

00:35:14.618 --> 00:35:16.254
Smash anything that moves.

00:35:27.610 --> 00:35:28.502
Crap.

00:35:47.036 --> 00:35:47.991
Hold on

00:35:48.246 --> 00:35:50.816
Whoa, guys, false alarm.

00:35:51.326 --> 00:35:52.473
I tripped the system.

00:35:52.590 --> 00:35:53.482
Who are you?

00:35:54.161 --> 00:35:55.266
I'm the boss's kid.

00:35:57.007 --> 00:35:58.452
You're Mr. Yamashiro's kid?

00:36:14.116 --> 00:36:15.199
Come on.

00:36:16.324 --> 00:36:17.535
Come into this one.

00:36:41.270 --> 00:36:42.321
It's your fault.

00:36:43.766 --> 00:36:44.849
You killed her.

00:36:48.566 --> 00:36:49.861
You killed Jessica.

00:36:53.492 --> 00:36:55.297
Like I said, I was adopted.

00:36:56.072 --> 00:36:56.858
Yeah.

00:36:59.577 --> 00:37:00.596
You know, I just

00:37:01.287 --> 00:37:03.432
I really don't have
timefor this right now.

00:37:09.485 --> 00:37:10.823
You never told her the truth,

00:37:11.513 --> 00:37:12.724
Who you really were.

00:37:13.467 --> 00:37:15.166
But it's more than that,isn't it?

00:37:16.122 --> 00:37:17.715
Those nightmares you've been having

00:37:18.150 --> 00:37:19.658
Of jessica dying,

00:37:20.104 --> 00:37:21.060
Screaming,

00:37:21.952 --> 00:37:22.823
Burning

00:37:23.524 --> 00:37:25.796
You had them for days before she died.

00:37:26.784 --> 00:37:27.804
Didn't you?!

00:37:30.352 --> 00:37:32.264
You were so desperateto ignore them,

00:37:32.285 --> 00:37:34.006
To believethey were just dreams.

00:37:34.664 --> 00:37:36.140
How could you ignore them like that?

00:37:36.777 --> 00:37:39.283
How could you leave her alone to die?

00:37:42.129 --> 00:37:43.786
You dreamt it would happen!

00:37:50.478 --> 00:37:51.264
Dude.

00:37:51.837 --> 00:37:53.281
Sammy, sammy!

00:37:55.161 --> 00:37:56.053
It's sam.

00:37:57.845 --> 00:37:59.035
God, are you okay?

00:37:59.226 --> 00:38:00.118
Uh, yeah.

00:38:02.157 --> 00:38:03.049
Come on, come on.

00:39:06.127 --> 00:39:08.272
You killed them!

00:39:08.718 --> 00:39:10.418
All those people!

00:39:10.803 --> 00:39:12.991
You killed them!

00:39:41.510 --> 00:39:42.402
Hey, sam?

00:39:43.332 --> 00:39:44.118
Yeah?

00:39:45.530 --> 00:39:48.674
That's got to be like
what, 600 years of bad luck?

00:40:13.039 --> 00:40:14.377
So this is really over?

00:40:16.227 --> 00:40:17.268
Yeah, it's over.

00:40:19.498 --> 00:40:20.348
Thank you.

00:40:32.261 --> 00:40:33.110
Charlie?

00:40:37.144 --> 00:40:38.546
Your boyfriend's death,

00:40:39.799 --> 00:40:41.561
You really should try
to forgive yourself.

00:40:42.326 --> 00:40:43.367
No matter what you did,

00:40:43.834 --> 00:40:45.066
You probably couldn't have stopped it.

00:40:47.561 --> 00:40:49.091
Sometimes bad things just happen.

00:41:00.775 --> 00:41:01.742
That's good advice.

00:41:18.272 --> 00:41:19.101
Hey, sam?

00:41:20.163 --> 00:41:20.800
Yeah?

00:41:21.788 --> 00:41:23.359
Now that this is all over,

00:41:24.336 --> 00:41:26.078
I want you to tell me
what that secret is.

00:41:31.016 --> 00:41:31.950
Look...

00:41:33.469 --> 00:41:34.467
You're my brother.

00:41:35.848 --> 00:41:37.165
And I'd die for you.

00:41:39.830 --> 00:41:41.869
But there are some things
I need to keep to myself.



00:00:05.500 --> 00:00:07.000
